[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two ceramic bowls centered on an aged, dark oak kitchen table, arranged in a 3/4 overhead perspective that allows for clear visibility of all ingredients. The foreground bowl is sharp, while the second is softly blurred behind it. Each serving contains a base of nutty-brown, textured brown rice topped with a generous, tender fillet of opaque, flaky white haddock. Beside the fish, vibrant, emerald-green wilted baby bok choy and bright, firm edamame beans are nestled, not stacked, ensuring each component is distinct. A light, translucent ginger-soy broth glazes the components, creating a subtle sheen on the surface. Fresh, thin slices of green scallions are scattered casually over the top. The lighting is soft, natural, and diffused from a window on the left, casting gentle, realistic shadows. Props include a rumpled, neutral-colored linen napkin tucked to the side and a small wooden spoon resting naturally on the table surface, along with a few stray green scallion slices and a tiny splash of broth on the rim of the bowl. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene reflects a home-cooked, lived-in warmth, with slight imperfections like an asymmetric garnish and an uneven texture to the wilted greens. The color temperature is a cozy, golden-hour amber. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry, no text, no watermarks, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from a professional cookbook photograph."
  }
]
